            <ArticleTitle>Prevalence of autoantibodies against contractile proteins in coronary artery disease and their clinical implications.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>870-2, A6, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this initial study, we found that autoantibodies against actin and myosin were present during and after an acute coronary syndrome. Moreover, they correlated with persistent troponin-I elevation at follow-up, and with late myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
